Scope the exported include root to <prefix>/include, not <prefix>/include/yoga.

Yoga's install interface publishes the yoga/ header directory ITSELF as a
public include root, so every consumer that links yoga::yogacore silently gains
algorithm/, config/, debug/, enums/, event/, node/, numeric/ and style/ as
top-level include prefixes. On a case-insensitive filesystem an engine module's
own "Event/Event.h" then resolves to yoga/event/event.h whenever the module's
include directory is searched after yoga's - and it is: the Editor's generated
include list carries yoga at position 32 with most module include directories
after it.

Deleting the entry rather than rewriting it, because the root it was meant to
provide is already exported and the two produced literal duplicates in
yogaTargets.cmake: the top-level CMakeLists installs yogacore with
INCLUDES DESTINATION ${CMAKE_INSTALL_INCLUDEDIR}, and every Yoga header includes
its siblings as <yoga/...>, so <prefix>/include is the only root Yoga needs.
(It was also absolute - ${CMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX} bakes the packaging prefix into
the exported target, which is why vcpkg's config fixup has to rewrite it.)

diff --git a/yoga/CMakeLists.txt b/yoga/CMakeLists.txt
--- a/yoga/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/yoga/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -37,5 +37,4 @@ endif()
 
 target_include_directories(yogacore
     PUBLIC
-    $<BUILD_INTERFACE:${YOGA_ROOT}>
-    $<INSTALL_INTERFACE:${CMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX}/include/yoga>)
+    $<BUILD_INTERFACE:${YOGA_ROOT}>)
